    "body": "Yes, I found that merging them together indeed results in simpler conflict checking rules.\r\n\r\nHowever, I would still like to raise the concern about the fact that Zicfiss occupies the MOP encoding space may one day result in the Zicfilp being selectively enabled without Zicfiss, if some valuable extension is to be redefined in the MOP encoding space and thus conflicts with Zicfiss. Besides, given that shadow stack has a software-based alternative implementation, substituting Zicfiss with the software alternative so MOP could be repurposed for some unique extension doesn't seem like a mad option to me.",
    "created_at": "2025-08-11T11:29:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-11T11:29:28Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/riscv-non-isa/riscv-elf-psabi-doc/pull/474#discussion_r2266424514",
